  "$comment": "One command source. `menus` is the native menu bar (src-tauri/src/menu.rs builds it; the custom title bar opens the same menus as popups): File (windows, folders, files), View (the rail items in rail order, Plans, then the Explorer and the data reload), Go (go to a file, a command, the active file, back and forward), Terminal, Run, Help. `config` is the action rows of Workspace → Config, which holds settings only (src/main.ts renders them after its Skin, Title bar and Rail choices; `omarchyOnly` rows show on Omarchy only); an id lives in exactly one of the two (menu.rs tests check it against the action map in src/main.ts, runAction), and the Commands palette lists both. No mnemonics (& or _) and no accelerators: GTK would take those keys from the terminals and the editor.",
